```
qualityFrames++;
qualityTime+=dt;
if (qualityTime >= 1.8) { avg=qualityTime/qualityFrames; ... reset }
```
This adapts within ~3.6s (warmup + 1.8) per step, 7s for two steps. Maybe too slow. Use warmup 0.8, window 1.2s. At 60fps 72 frames. Fine. One janky frame at 50ms over 72 = avg 0.017, no trigger. Threshold 0.022. Good.
Start monitor immediately at boot. Title at DPR1.5 headless 20fps => after 2s lower 1.25; after 2s lower 1.0; before user likely starts? They may click in 1s. But real phone no. If user starts immediately, gameplay adapts.

Should we lower only if frame avg > 0.023 and at least e.g. 30 frames? At 20fps, 1.2s=24 frames. Enough. Use 24 min.

Could also lower if avg > 0.027. At DPR1.25 35fps avg .0286 -> lower to 1.0. Good. At DPR1.5 20fps .05 -> lower. Threshold 0.024 (~41fps). Good.

After lowering, do not increase automatically. Stable.

Need `resize()` resets stats and maybe show toast? no.
